        "topicId": "math-y9-simultaneous-equations",
        "provisionalConceptFamily": "ratio-transfer",
        "stem": "Boxes A and B initially contain unknown positive whole numbers of counters. Moving 15 counters from A to B makes their counts have ratio 2:3. Instead, starting from the original counts, moving 6 counters from B to A makes the ratio 3:2. Find the original total number of counters.",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "latex": "150",
            "errorPath": "Incorrectly assume the original boxes held equal counts, then use only the first transfer: T/2−15=2T/5 gives T=150."
          },
          {
            "id": "B",
            "latex": "21",
            "errorPath": "Report the difference between the two values of A after the transfers."
          },
          {
            "id": "C",
            "latex": "57",
            "errorPath": "Report A's original count."
          },
          {
            "id": "D",
            "latex": "48",
            "errorPath": "Report B's original count."
          },
          {
            "id": "E",
            "latex": "5",
            "errorPath": "Report the sum of the ratio parts."
          },
          {
            "id": "F",
            "latex": "105"
          }
        ],
        "correctOptionId": "F",
        "correctAnswerLatex": "105",
        "workedSolutionSteps": [
          "Let T=A+B. The first operation gives A−15=2T/5; the second gives A+6=3T/5.",
          "Subtract: 21=T/5, so T=105.",
          "Then A=57,B=48; both transfers are possible and the two ratios are satisfied."
